# Example environment for local development. Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in,
# OR export these in your shell profile. NEVER commit real values — see SECURITY.md.

# Auth token for the private Hugeicons Pro npm registry (@hugeicons-pro/*).
# Required for `npm ci` / `npm install` to succeed. The committed `.npmrc` reads
# it as ${NPM_TOKEN}. Get the value from the team secret manager (1Password:
# "Hugeicons Pro npm token"). See the "Prerequisites" section in README.md.
#
# Note: npm reads this from the process environment, so it must be exported in
# your shell (e.g. via ~/.zshrc, Keychain-backed on macOS) before installing —
# a `.env` file alone is not read by npm during install.
NPM_TOKEN=
